<div class="callout"><div class="ct">Standing caveats on every dollar on this card</div><p><strong>Every repriced number is a CEILING.</strong> Fills are modelled at the exact stop/target/trail level with no slippage, and the desk's own standing finding is that live losses run <strong>1.1&ndash;3.1&times; modelled</strong>. Treat the policy as the edge and the headline dollar as decoration. Anything on thin n is flagged in-row as a <em>direction</em>, not a measurement.</p><p><strong>The fee is $1.50 per round trip and the multipliers are not the same.</strong> MNQ is $2.00 a point; <strong>MGC is $10.00</strong>. Every gold number in Movement 3 and in Part 2.5 Part A is priced at the gold multiplier &mdash; pricing gold with the Nasdaq one would understate it fivefold, and doing the reverse would flatter it fivefold.</p><p><strong>Four method wounds are open and they bound everything above.</strong> <code>signal_journal.suppressed_by</code> is NULL in all 222 rows this week, so every claim about what a gate <em>would</em> have done unrouted is a reconstruction from the tape rather than a measurement &mdash; and it is the <em>same defect the scope flagged last week</em> &mdash; <strong>BUILD&nbsp;#9</strong>. The router&rsquo;s leakage detector is scoped to a universe that barely trades (<code>capitulation_long</code> and <code>rgv_short</code>), so its zero is an empty set and not a clean week &mdash; <code>exhaustion_short</code> leaked &minus;$241 unseen &mdash; <strong>BUILD&nbsp;#10</strong>. The nightly rollup reports $0/$0/$0 when the systemd journal has rotated past the day it is backfilling, which is indistinguishable from a day with no value &mdash; <strong>BUILD&nbsp;#10</strong>. <code>selector_nightly</code> counted a quarantined trade four extra times, inflating one day&rsquo;s regret by 39% ($747.50 &rarr; $457.50 on 10 real trades) &mdash; the phantom is FOUR rows worth $290.00, not five worth $362.50; the fifth day-rider row that day is the genuine claimed trade and must survive the fix &mdash; <strong>BUILD&nbsp;#11</strong>.</p><p><strong>What did not run this cycle, named exactly.</strong> The rehabilitation phase timed out, and Part 1.5 was rebuilt from the artifacts it had already saved. In Movement 3 the four <em>per-cause-cluster</em> hunts did not run &mdash; <code>gf_full_FLOW-LED.md</code>, <code>gf_full_OPEN-NEWS.md</code>, <code>gf_full_UNCLASS.md</code> and <code>gf_full_RIDER_ALL.md</code> on disk are all dated 15 August, i.e. last week&rsquo;s artifacts, and nothing stitched them in. <strong>The rest of Movement 3 is fresh and ran tonight:</strong> the VACUUM cluster hunt, the 686-run lake study, the three forward tests, BIGBOARD, SMALLFADE, LOTDIV and the chop lab all ran 2026-08-22 00:00&ndash;00:39. So this is not &ldquo;you got no MNQ greenfield work this week&rdquo; &mdash; it is four cluster hunts missing from a movement that otherwise delivered. <strong>Nothing on this card rests on a section that is missing.</strong></p></div>
