<h4 class="dr">Read the closed-book row, and read winners-kept beside it</h4>

<p><strong>1.5&times;ATR is the fourth-best of seven widths and it LOSES money on the closed book.</strong>
It takes the rider from &minus;$272.00 to &minus;$388.90 &mdash; $116.90 <em>worse</em> than doing
nothing &mdash; because 41.4pt is inside Monday&rsquo;s &minus;75.25pt excursion and 46.4pt is inside
Tuesday&rsquo;s &minus;64.50pt, so it converts a +$453 winner into &minus;$168.60 and a +$185 winner
into &minus;$188.40. It keeps <strong>one of the three winners</strong>.</p>

<p><strong>3.0&times;ATR is the pick, and it is the only width that is both.</strong> On the closed book it
is <strong>+$195.70</strong> &mdash; the only positive cell in the row &mdash; and it is the only width
that keeps <strong>all three</strong> winners, because 82.8 / 92.7 / 105.9pt all sit outside Monday,
Tuesday and Wednesday&rsquo;s worst excursions. It still caps Thursday at &minus;$826.80 against
&minus;$1,294.50. Against as-traded that is <strong>+$467.70 on the closed book</strong>, and
<strong>+$703.90</strong> once the open carry is marked in.</p>

<div class="callout"><div class="ct">&#9733; AND THE THING NEITHER REVISION EXPECTED &mdash; ANY stop closes the weekend carry</div>
<p>Every one of the seven widths stops Friday&rsquo;s 13:13Z entry, and all of them do it within
<strong>nineteen minutes</strong>: 0.5&times; at 13:13:06, 1.0&times; at 13:16:54, 1.5&times; at 13:20:49,
3.0&times; at 13:31:55 for &minus;$742.80. The gateway did not wedge until <strong>19:57Z</strong>.
So the four lots that are the headline of this report, the ones that need a Sunday-night gateway check
and a weekend-flatten timer, would not exist under any stop this section tested. The carry is a
<em>missing-stop</em> incident that a wedge then made unfixable &mdash; not a wedge incident.</p>
<p class="drnote">One honest artefact: at 0.5&times;ATR the stop (29,476.28) sits <em>inside the
position&rsquo;s own fill spread</em> &mdash; the fills were 2 @ 29,477.00 and 2 @ 29,506.25, a 29.25pt
spread around a 29,491.625 VWAP &mdash; so it triggers in the entry second. That is a real property of
stopping a badly-filled position off its VWAP, not a simulator bug, and it is one more reason not to
pick the tightest cell.</p></div>

<div class="callout"><div class="ct">What this does NOT license</div>
<p><strong>Six rider entries is not a sample.</strong> Three winners decide the winners-kept column and
one of them (Wednesday) survives every width from 1.0&times; up, so the ranking between 1.0&times; and
3.0&times; rests on Monday and Tuesday alone. The closed-book row is the verdict-bearing one precisely
because every leg in it is resolved; the row beneath it contains a position that is <strong>still
open</strong>, and a marked-to-market leg can only be scored at its current excursion, never at its
eventual exit &mdash; so treat that row as provisional and re-cut it the moment the carry closes.
The instruction that survives all of this is not &ldquo;3.0&times;&rdquo;, it is <strong>&ldquo;have a
stop, and never pick its width from the losing day&rdquo;</strong>.</p></div>

