forgotten.</p>

<h3>Disposition &mdash; every lead this section touched</h3><table><thead><tr><th class="ln">Lead</th><th class="ln">Verdict</th><th class="ln">For PARKED: what would revive it. For REFUTED: the test that killed it.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="ln"><strong>Arm grind only on clean-trend days</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED</span></td><td class="ln">It is not refuted &mdash; it makes $580.50 gross against a &minus;$958.00 gross control and keeps 25 of 43 winners. It is un-runnable: only 1 of 240 sessions is both clean-trend and above the 22-point floor. <strong>&#9733; REV2 adds two things and neither revives it.</strong> Net of fees the rule is +$548.00 and <strong>2026-07-29 alone is +$634.50 of it on 46 fires</strong> &mdash; drop that one session and the other eight days are &minus;$1,784.50, so &ldquo;the best rule on the board&rdquo; and &ldquo;arm on 2026-07-29&rdquo; are nearly the same instruction on this sample. And the BUILDING-block version of the idea, scored on the same 128 fires with Movement&nbsp;3&nbsp;&sect;8's own classifier, is <strong>&minus;$748.50 on 51 fires keeping 17 of 43 winners</strong> &mdash; worse per fire than no rule at all, so it is not parked behind the wrong condition. The floor question below is answered too, and it does not revive this either.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>grind&#x27;s 22-point ATR floor as a number</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-shadow">SHADOW</span></td><td class="ln"><strong>&#9733; REV2 &mdash; ASKED AND ANSWERED, tonight, on the 128 live fires (&sect;2b).</strong> The ladder is monotone upward &mdash; 14pt &minus;$1,143.50 &rarr; 22pt &minus;$280.50 &rarr; 28pt +$469.00 &mdash; but <strong>strip-best-3 is negative at every rung and the worst leave-one-day-out is negative at every rung</strong>, and against 5,000 random same-size subsets the live 22pt rung sits at only the 65th percentile. Cause of death: strip-best-3 and leave-one-day-out. Raising the floor cannot make grind positive on its own live record, so this is no longer &ldquo;the real grind question&rdquo; &mdash; grind is an entry question. Keep the shadow arms as a forward confirmation of the monotone shape, nothing more. Reachability is also resolved: 22pt is the p75 of SESSION minutes and the p89 of ALL minutes; the two published figures were one denominator apart, not two measurements.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>Fix grind with an ER floor or a directional-net requirement</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED</span></td><td class="ln">Named test: nine cells across two families on 128 live fires, every one negative, including the ER-0.35 floor that is already deployed.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>MGC coil &mdash; fade the edge (or break it)</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED</span></td><td class="ln">Named test: a mirror control that also loses, and a placebo that 0 random sets failed to beat from below on 2,487 trades.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>MGC coil, tightest-compression cell only</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED</span></td><td class="ln">$962.00 on n=2,487. Revive by running the SAME placebo the full-sample arm got and holding out a year of tape. Until then it is the best of nine cells on data that produced a null.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>MGC 5&amp;times;ATR stop / hold-to-clock</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED</span></td><td class="ln">Monotone plateau, which is the shape of a real effect, but strip-best-3 takes $3,352.71 to &minus;$556.29. Revive at n&ge;200 sessions or on a second instrument.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>The MGC derived-trigger rider</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED</span></td><td class="ln">Out-of-sample $655.00, which is real, against a $20,382 always-short drift on the same window. Revive only with the long/short mix reported beside it.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>Report the long/short mix on every gold arm</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-live">LIVE</span></td><td class="ln">A method fix, not a strategy. Without it every gold number on this desk is confounded with a large short drift, and this section found two arms already reading it as edge.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>The open-rider &amp;lsquo;inside the window&amp;rsquo; session filter</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED</span></td><td class="ln">Named test: strip-best-3 takes $825.00 to &minus;$7,745.00 on 60 sessions. Three sessions are the whole lead.</td></tr><tr><td class="ln"><strong>The stay-out meter as a DIRECTION signal</strong></td><td class="ln"><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED</span></td><td class="ln">51.7% hit rate over 178 sessions when both reads agree. Its up/down asymmetry is the market's short drift, not the meter's skill. It stays in service as a stay-out instrument, which is what it was built to be.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
