<table><tr><th>Do this</th><th>Why</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td><strong>1. Retire <code>rider_w5</code> from the shadow book.</strong></td><td>It is the only item here that costs nothing and is decided. 51 forward trades, &minus;$28.84 each, red in every ATR bucket including the one its own filter selects for. It has been running unwatched since 08-17 because nobody graded it.</td><td><span class='why'>RIDER_ALL &sect;5</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>2. Build the MGC depth-mid bar source, then let both gold arms run.</strong></td><td>This is the gating item for the entire gold programme and it is mechanical &mdash; the shadow service already holds the <code>DepthFeed</code> it needs. Keep the trade-bar arms alive as <code>*_tradebar</code> controls so the next reader can see the difference rather than take it on trust.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;12.1</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>3. Fix the census's flow-bucket phase, and rename two labels.</strong></td><td>21 of 68 labels move on bucket phase alone. Then <code>UNCLASS</code> &rarr; <code>UNTESTED</code> and <code>OPEN/NEWS</code> &rarr; <code>US-OPEN-WINDOW</code> with the two anti-predictive footprint tests deleted. Three labs reached this independently and it is the cheapest correction on the list.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;13, OPEN/NEWS &sect;15, FLOW-LED VERDICT</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>4. Price the violent-whipsaw bench.</strong></td><td>The chop commission's premise was wrong &mdash; the tournament did not trade this week's chop days at all. Its money is lost in violent-whipsaw blocks, and a two-term bench there is worth roughly ten times the scalper that was commissioned to fix the wrong thing.</td><td><span class='why'>chopscalp &sect;2</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>5. Add <code>atr_min</code>, the wrapping clock window and an ER10 gate param to <code>ShadowVariant</code>.</strong></td><td>Three small changes, and they are a prerequisite for shadowing anything from this movement honestly. &#9733; This is exactly how <code>rider_w5</code> came to be quoted at +$19.29 while making &minus;$28.84: an arm shipped around a missing field records a DIFFERENT strategy under the same name.</td><td><span class='why'>RIDER_ALL &sect;11</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>6. Do NOT arm anything on MNQ out of this movement.</strong></td><td>Seven hunts, dozens of candidates, and not one MNQ LIVE candidate. That is the honest answer and it is stated plainly rather than dressed as a near-miss.</td><td><span class='why'>the whole movement</span></td></tr></table>
<h3 id="m3-dispo">10. Disposition &mdash; every lead this movement touched</h3>
<p>Four dispositions, one each. <strong>PARKED</strong> names the specific thing that would revive it; <strong>REFUTED</strong> names the test and why no reformulation saves it. Nothing here is a graveyard &mdash; a PARKED row is a lead with a stated price.</p>
<table><tr><th>Lead</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Required note</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td><strong>MGC shadow bar source</strong></td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">BUILD REQUIRED</span></td><td>The gating item for the whole gold line. Point the shadow's bar builder at the depth mid and keep the trade-bar arms as <code>*_tradebar</code> controls. The service already holds the <code>DepthFeed</code>. Nothing else on the gold line is worth doing first.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;3, &sect;12.1</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>mgc_hole_break_fade</code> LONG + SHORT + double-hole</td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">SHADOW</span></td><td>Survived the forward walk on the lab tape (+$512 / +$656, placebo 0/30, mirror and both constants negative, 3&ndash;4 ticks of slippage headroom). Losing in live shadow on production's tape (&minus;$256 over 14 trades) &mdash; that is the bar source, not the gate. Promote the double-hole arm to full status behind the fix.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;14</span></td></tr><tr><td>Cross-asset MNQ <strong>veto</strong> for gold</td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">SHADOW &mdash; new arm</span></td><td>+$5.43/tr against +$1.72 blanket over 278 paired days, two-sided, placebo at the 97th/2.5th percentile. Does <em>not</em> reproduce on the 29-day book window (34th pctile). Needs a new <code>_entry</code> branch and an MNQ state feed. Settle it by running it alongside.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;6</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>mgc_wall_break_go</code> LONG + SHORT</td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">SHADOW, on probation</span></td><td>Forward-walked +$693, mirror negative, filter placebo 0/200 &mdash; but fails the random-minute placebo 29/30 for the SECOND week, and strip-best-10 is &minus;$192. Promote no further until n &ge; 150 with a passing random-minute placebo.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;14</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>board_overnight</code> (21:00&ndash;07:00Z)</td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">SHADOW &mdash; an instrumented question</span></td><td>Right sign in two independent samples (+0.444R and +0.224R), counter-trend leg negative in both, survives a full point of slippage. But its daytime and counter-trend controls REVERSE on the held-out sample and its placebo p is 0.097. &#9733; <strong>Shadow it to answer a question, not because we think it makes money</strong> &mdash; and it needs three code changes first (a wrapping clock window, an <code>atr_min</code> field, and ER10 rather than ER30).</td><td><span class='why'>RIDER_ALL &sect;10, &sect;11</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>BENCH 07:00&ndash;13:00Z for any late-boarding rider</strong></td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">SHADOW &rarr; adopt as a router rule</span></td><td>Red on all three independent legs (&minus;$29.38 / &minus;$20.04 / &minus;$2.43, the last on n=373). Cheap, fail-safe direction, no new instrument needed. The cleanest positive deliverable in the movement.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;11, &sect;13</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>The violent-whipsaw bench</strong></td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">MEASURE, then route</span></td><td>The premise of the chop commission was wrong and the correction is worth more than the scalper. Across 18 days the tournament's loss is concentrated in <strong>violent-whipsaw</strong> blocks (&minus;$1,383.50 on 95 trades), NOT in plain chop (&minus;$403.00 on 58) &mdash; and on this week's two chop days the tournament took <strong>zero</strong> trades. A two-term router bench, worth roughly ten times the scalper it replaces.</td><td><span class='why'>chopscalp &sect;2, &sect;13</span></td></tr><tr><td>ER30 as a router ARM meter</td><td><span class="tag pill-shadow">SHADOW as an instrumented question</span></td><td>+$3.54 against &minus;$3.40 a trade on 3,238 untouched trades &mdash; the largest-n effect in the movement &mdash; but it REVERSES on the recent 11 sessions. Shadow the meter with its own control arm; do not arm a gate behind it.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;13</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>board_atrband</code></td><td><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED</span></td><td>Revive only with a SELECTOR &mdash; something that predicts which board becomes a run. NOT more days: the power calculation says ~10,500 trades to separate it from zero.</td><td><span class='why'>RIDER_ALL &sect;10</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>UNCL-RIDE-ER</code></td><td><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED</span></td><td>Revive only with a board-time SIZE PREDICTOR expressed in ATRs (r &ge; 0.4 against eventual run size on &ge; 300 runs). More days will not fix it &mdash; 205 untouched sessions were already spent and the placebo won.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;13</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>mgc_coil_bounce</code></td><td><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED (updated)</span></td><td>Last week killed it partly on the <strong>$7.50 cost error</strong>; at the corrected $4.50 the 08-15 audit puts it at +$8.42 &mdash; breakeven rather than dead. Not re-derived this week. Revive by re-running it on the 29-day quote tape at the corrected cost.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;14</span></td></tr><tr><td>Lookback 90/120 min (gold)</td><td><span class="tag pill-parked">PARKED</span></td><td>The year's monotone gradient does not survive the book gate. 45&ndash;180 min is a plateau; leave it at 60.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;5.2</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>rider_w5</code> (live shadow arm)</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED &mdash; RETIRE THE ARM</span></td><td>51 live forward trades at &minus;$28.84/tr, red in all four ATR buckets; 1,339 OOS trades at &minus;$5.43/tr with strip-3 at &minus;$9,293; &minus;$174 on the census week it was built for; and its in-sample +$1,936 collapses to +$282 on strip-best-3.</td><td><span class='why'>RIDER_ALL &sect;5</span></td></tr><tr><td><code>UNCL-RIDER-ASIA</code></td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED &mdash; do not re-shadow</span></td><td>Four consecutive red forward weeks. &#9733; And it was <strong>never actually shipped</strong> &mdash; there is no arm by that name anywhere in <code>shadow.db</code>, which nobody had noticed.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;9</span></td></tr><tr><td>The <code>VACUUM</code> / <code>FLOW-LED</code> split</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED as a footprint &mdash; STOP SPLITTING</span></td><td>The flow event fires on 20.4&ndash;20.6% of all tape and then splits it on a <strong>49.6&ndash;49.9% coin toss</strong> &mdash; 0.33 percentage points of directional information. The lift the flow event does carry is a MAGNITUDE lift and it is a volume proxy.</td><td><span class='why'>FLOW-LED &sect;0, VACUUM &sect;2</span></td></tr><tr><td>The <code>UNCLASS</code> label</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED as a footprint &mdash; RENAME</span></td><td>Base rate 73.9% on the census week, 75.4% on the whole lake, lift <strong>0.82</strong>; its members sit ON the all-tape median for ATR, volume and efficiency. Rename it <code>UNTESTED</code> and report it as COVERAGE. Second independent measurement in two weeks.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;1, &sect;13</span></td></tr><tr><td>The <code>OPEN/NEWS</code> label</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">FIX &mdash; drop the footprint tests</span></td><td>Its lift over the BARE CLOCK is <strong>0.921&times;</strong>: the flow and amplitude tests remove 41% of the window and keep the <em>less</em> run-dense half. Either call it <code>US-OPEN-WINDOW</code> (3.09&times; lift on 8.87% of tape) or route the hunt through <code>VOL-EXPANSION</code> &mdash; 4.18&times; lift on 1.95% of tape, the sharpest cluster the census produces and the one it uses least.</td><td><span class='why'>OPEN/NEWS &sect;1, &sect;15</span></td></tr><tr><td>The census's flow-bucket PHASE</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">FIX &mdash; this is a real bug</span></td><td>21 of 68 labels change on bucket phase alone, and only 17 of 68 run timestamps are minute-aligned. Snap the window slide to the CLOCK, not to the array index.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;13</span></td></tr><tr><td>The lake <code>bars</code> timeframe landmine</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">FIX REQUIRED</span></td><td>Backfill parquet at 1min/5mins/1hour/1day now sits beside the daily 5s files; any query without a <code>timeframe</code> filter inherits up to a full day of look-ahead on every day.</td><td><span class='why'>MGC &sect;14</span></td></tr><tr><td>L2 far-side depletion as a run selector</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED (two independent measurements)</span></td><td>RIDER_ALL: 311 fires, 264M book rows, r = &minus;0.009, placebo p = 0.62. VACUUM: 49.44% &plusmn;2.52pp on unselected 55pt+ moves over 246.9M book rows, and 49.72% &plusmn;0.67pp on all 21,249 book-minutes. <strong>Do not revive it at 30 days &mdash; the null is not n-limited.</strong></td><td><span class='why'>RIDER_ALL &sect;7, VACUUM &sect;6</span></td></tr><tr><td>The far-side WALL as an absorption tell</td><td><span class="tag pill-dontarm">REFUTED, with the sign INVERTED</span></td><td>The operator's core L2 hypothesis. Unfiltered chop turns drift +0.054pt in the fade's favour; requiring a wall &ge;1.5&times; turns that to &minus;0.117pt, and five-deep &ge;1.3&times; to &minus;0.374pt (t = &minus;1.72, quintile z = &minus;2.37). <strong>The wall is a TARGET, not absorption.</strong></td><td><span class='why'>chopscalp &sect;3</span></td></tr><tr><td>The four run SHAPES (TURN / STEP-REPRICE / DRIFT-VOID / GRIND-CONT)</td><td><span class="tag pill-live">SHIP TO THE CENSUS</span></td><td>One <code>if</code> each, all computable at the run's start minute. Not a selector &mdash; vocabulary, to replace the three labels that just died.</td><td><span class='why'>UNCLASS &sect;10</span></td></tr><tr><td>The 41ms refill count</td><td><span class="tag pill-live">KEEP &mdash; the one L2 term that ever helped</span><