<h5>6. THE LAST LEAD — THE OVERNIGHT LEG, AND WHY IT DID NOT REPLICATE</h5>
<p>One thing did survive the out-of-sample leg, and I chased it as far as it goes.</p>
<p>Splitting the 1,289 OOS boards by session. ⚠ This is a post-hoc split of an entry set built <em>without</em> a session constraint, so the 60-minute lockout falls differently than it does when the session is part of the rule — the session-constrained run below gives n=396 and +$10.46/trade rather than the n=383 and +$11.50 here. Same finding, slightly different bookkeeping; I quote the session-constrained numbers everywhere it matters.</p>
