<h6>Its router rule, in the router's own vocabulary</h6>
<blockquote><strong>ARM <code>board_overnight_band</code> when, and only when, all four are true at the tick:</strong> 1. the clock is between <strong>21:00 and 07:00 UTC</strong>; 2. the router's own <strong>ATR meter reads 11.0 to 16.0 points</strong> (this is the mean 1-min range over 20 minutes — the number the router already prints; it is a <strong>band</strong>, so bench it <em>above</em> 16 as well as below 11); 3. <strong>RUN STATE is RUN or RUN-FADING</strong> — the arm is a boarding rule and has no business firing in declared chop; 4. the <strong>untradeable meter is clear</strong> and the tape is not inside a scheduled gateway window (04:28–05:00Z sits squarely inside this arm's session and hangs with the port open). <strong>BENCH it immediately if the ATR meter leaves the band in either direction</strong>, and treat a bench here as cheap: the arm's whole thesis is that both edges of the band carry weight. <strong>Expectancy on the home regime only</strong> (overnight, ATR 11–16, wide exit): <strong>+$10.46 a trade on the 236-session generating sample, +$5.34 a trade on the 28-session held-out sample.</strong> Take the <em>lower</em> of those as the working expectation, and note that its own strip-best-3 on the held-out sample is −$51 — three trades were the whole thing. <strong>This is not a number to size on.</strong></blockquote>
<h6>Promotion bar — deliberately set high</h6>
<p>Do <strong>not</strong> promote this to the paper tournament on P&amp;L alone. It needs <strong>all four</strong>:</p>
<ol><li><strong>200 shadow trades</strong>, including at least one genuinely trending overnight week;</li><li><strong>≥ +0.15R</strong> over those trades <strong>after</strong> stripping its best three;</li><li>the <strong>daytime control arm</strong> (identical rule, 13:00–20:00Z) must be <strong>materially worse</strong> — that is the claim under test, and it is the one that failed to replicate;</li><li>the <strong>counter-trend control</strong> must stay negative. It reversed on the held-out lake, and if it reverses again the arm is measuring noise and should be retired without argument.</li></ol>
<p><strong>I would also add the daytime control arm at the same time.</strong> Shadowing the treatment without the control is what produced this week's ambiguity in the first place.</p>
