<h4>GREENFIELD HUNT — CLUSTER <code>UNCLASS</code></h4>
<h6>MNQ · full parquet lake · 5s tape 2026-06-19 → 08-24 (51 sessions) + a 205-session 1-minute leg back to 2025-09-14 · $2.00/point · <strong>$1.50 per round trip</strong></h6>
<hr class="frag-sep">
<h5>THE SHORT VERSION, BEFORE ANY OF THE WORKING</h5>
<p>Garrath — I did the three steps in the order you set them. I built a direction-agnostic run-catcher and rode the UNCLASS runs without needing to know why they happened. I swept the exit far wider than the desk has ever run one. I filtered it with a causal rule and placebo-controlled every cut against throwing away the same number of fires at random. Then I routed it. It still lost.</p>
<p><strong>It died on the PLACEBO/SHUFFLE TEST, corroborated by the OUT-OF-SAMPLE LEG.</strong> On the biggest independent sample I have — 205 sessions of tape that chose nothing — the real signal makes <strong>+$3.54 a trade</strong> and the <strong>fake signal, taken thirty minutes early with every other rule untouched, makes +$4.44 a trade</strong>. On the recent forward leg the real signal makes <strong>−$9.58 a trade</strong> and the fake one makes <strong>+$1.48</strong>. When a shifted copy of your signal outperforms your signal on two independent samples, you do not have a signal — and per your judging rule that is the named cause of death, not the 25% win rate, which I have deliberately ignored throughout.</p>
<p>Four things came out of the week that are worth more than the dead rider:</p>
<ol><li><strong>UNCLASS is not a cluster and this is now measured twice, independently.</strong> I evaluated the census's own waterfall on <strong>every one of the 6,784 minutes</strong> of its window. UNCLASS is true on <strong>73.9% of the tape</strong> and takes <strong>60.3% of the runs</strong> — a <strong>lift of 0.82</strong>. A label with a lift <em>below</em> 1.0 is not a footprint. It is the null hypothesis with a name tag, and "UNCLASS: 41 runs" reads as a discovery when it means "41 runs happened somewhere in the three-quarters of the week we have no test for."</li><li><strong>And it is worse than last week thought: 21 of the 68 labels flip on nothing but where a minute starts.</strong> I changed <em>one</em> thing — the phase of the 60-second flow buckets — and 31% of the census's cluster assignments changed. Only 17 of 68 run timestamps are minute-aligned, so this is not a hypothetical.</li><li><strong>Last week's survivor was never shipped, and the tape since has buried it.</strong> <code>UNCL-RIDER-ASIA</code> went to SHADOW on 2026-08-15 and no arm by that name exists in <code>shadow.db</code>. I replayed it myself. It is now <strong>four consecutive red weeks</strong>, and the newest week — pure forward tape it has never seen — is <strong>−$472 over 16 trades, −$29.51 a trade, 18.8% wins</strong>. The drawdown that made it a non-deploy last week did not recover; it deepened.</li><li><strong>The prize is not $5,840.</strong> A boarder that fires inside every UNCLASS run and then exits at the <em>exact top of each move with no costs at all</em> reaches <strong>$3,239 — 55%</strong>. Put an honest stop on it and bank half the excursion and it is <strong>$1,592, 27%</strong>. Two thirds of the headline is a close-to-close number that no late entry can ever collect.</li></ol>
<p>The full ledger of every attempt — thirteen named candidates, none of them quietly dropped — is at the bottom, along with the two things I <em>do</em> want to carry forward, both of which are router instruments rather than gates.</p>
