<p>On 3,238 trades of untouched tape the efficiency meter turns a losing rider into a marginally positive one — that is a large sample and a real effect, and it is the <em>only</em> thing in this document with that kind of n behind it. On the most recent eleven sessions it makes things worse. I am reporting both and recommending neither as a deploy.</p>
<h6>The instrument we would actually need</h6>
<p>The binding constraint is named precisely in §8: <strong>a SIZE PREDICTOR at board time, in ATR units.</strong> Every board-time read we own — ATR, volume, efficiency, thrust size, and (per last week's L2 work, which I did not re-dig) depth imbalance — correlates with a run's eventual size in ATRs at r ≤ 0.13, except thrust-in-ATRs at +0.48, which is already a swept parameter with no gradient. Until something answers "given the volatility, is this going to be a 3-ATR move or a 12-ATR move", this rider risks a 2-ATR stop to collect a median 2.57 ATRs and the arithmetic never closes. <strong>That is a missing instrument, not a failed strategy, and it is what the next attempt should go and build.</strong></p>
