<h6>2.2 Why I did not backtest on ten runs</h6>
<p>Ten runs over five days cannot support a robustness battery, and <code>capture.db</code> — which is what the census reads — is a <strong>5-trading-day rolling window</strong>. Anything I fit on it would be fit on the sample. So the hunt runs on the <strong>full parquet lake</strong>:</p>
<pre><code>[lake] MNQ 5s bars: 438,253 rows, 2026-07-16 00:00 → 2026-08-21 20:59 UTC
       27 trading days · typical 15-min range = 44.2pt · run threshold = 1.5× = 66.4pt
       405 runs ≥ threshold · 60 of them OPEN/NEWS</code></pre>
<p>The lake's threshold (66.4pt) is stricter than the frozen week's (55pt) because the lake's typical 15-min range is wider (44.2 vs 37pt). I kept the census's own arithmetic rather than pinning the number, so the run definition is the census's definition on every day it is applied to.</p>
<p><strong>60 <code>OPEN/NEWS</code> runs on 26 of 27 days</strong> — 32 UP, 28 DN, 32 in hour 13 and 28 in hour 14, sizes 68pt to 234pt. No minute-of-hour concentration at all (the busiest single minute has 3 of 60, and 13:30 — the cash open itself — has 2). <strong>Whatever this bucket is, it is not a news-release footprint.</strong></p>
<h6>2.3 The unit and the costs</h6>
<ul><li><strong>U = 44.0pt</strong> — median 15-min hi-lo range, computed <em>causally</em> (trailing 24h rolling median), so no config knows the future. This is the census's own "typical 15-min range" statistic.</li><li><strong>$2.00 / point</strong> (MNQ; MGC is $10 and is not in this section).</li><li><strong>$1.50 per ROUND TRIP.</strong> Grepped the harness before reuse per the contract: <code>engine.py: TICK, VPP, FEE = 0.25, 2.00, 1.50</code> and <code>net = gross - FEE</code> charged <strong>once per trade</strong>. Not $5 (which would have killed every marginal candidate on a fee 3.3× too high), not per side.</li><li><strong>1 tick (0.25pt) adverse slippage</strong> on every stop-entry and every stop-exit.</li><li><strong>Pessimistic intrabar</strong>: within a 5s bar the stop is checked <strong>before</strong> the target. A bar that touches both is scored a loss.</li></ul>
<h6>2.4 Tick-honesty audit of the fills</h6>
<p>The harness runs on 5s OHLC, so I audited the fills against the <strong>tick tape</strong> (memory: <em>"a wrong-instrument tape PASSES the stop-width sweep"</em> — consistency is not correctness).</p>
