<p>The 13:00–15:00Z window essentially <strong>never coils</strong>. To get a usable n you must relax the compression test until it stops meaning compression (q=0.75 is a 33pt 15-minute range — barely below the 44pt median). And at q=0.60 the whole $492.50 is three trades (156% of net; strip-3 = −$46.00, i.e. every survivor is a stop) and the <strong>long side loses on every one of its trades</strong> while the short side makes $105/tr — n=9 split 2/7. <strong>Cause of death: n, and parameter sweep — the edge exists only where the compression test has been relaxed into meaninglessness.</strong></p>
<h6>4.3 PULSE — 1-minute impulse continuation</h6>
<p>Trigger: a 1-minute close-to-close move ≥ k×U inside 13–15Z. Direction = the impulse's sign. Entry: stop order 1 tick beyond that minute's extreme. This is the largest-n candidate on the page and got the fullest battery — §5.</p>
<h6>4.4 FADE1 — the exact mirror — <strong>−$13.05/tr</strong></h6>
<p>Identical trigger, direction reversed, market entry. −$13.05/tr over 211. Not a failure so much as a <strong>control that passed</strong>: PULSE's +$11.35 and FADE1's −$13.05 are close to symmetric around −$1.50 of fee, which says the two are genuine mirrors and the harness is not manufacturing money from the entry mechanics. That matters — it means PULSE's direction rule is doing <em>something</em>. §5.4 shows it is not doing enough.</p>
<h6>4.5 RNGX60 — 60-minute structure break — <strong>−$12.02/tr</strong></h6>
<p>Two-sided break of the trailing 60-minute high/low. 216 events, 81 triggers. Negative raw, negative at every strip, negative on both sides. <strong>Cause of death: negative expectancy, unconditionally.</strong> By 13:00Z the 60-minute extremes are the overnight range's edges, and MNQ spends the US open chopping across them.</p>
<h6>4.6 VWRC — session-VWAP cross — <strong>−$8.59/tr</strong></h6>
<p>Enter in the direction of a cross back through the running session VWAP. 42 events, 41 trades, −$8.59/tr, negative both sides, −$24.46 after strip-3. <code>d_vwap</code> had already scored <strong>AUC 0.494</strong> for direction in §3.1 — a coin. <strong>Cause of death: negative expectancy; predicted by the direction AUC.</strong></p>
<h6>4.7 OAB — volume-ignition two-sided break — <strong>no parameter plateau</strong></h6>
<p>The first gate built deliberately on the §1.5 orthogonal channel. Arm when raw 1-minute <strong>volume z</strong> ≥ V <em>and</em> |flow z| &lt; 1 — a <strong>two-sided auction</strong>: heavy trade, balanced aggression, exactly the state the census's net-flow instrument is blind to. Then a two-sided break of the 5-minute range.</p>
<p>The arm itself is real (§3, and lift 1.66× at vol_z&gt;2.5 even restricted to flow-quiet minutes). The gate is not. <strong>192-cell sweep</strong> over V ∈ {1.0,1.5,2.0,2.5} × wait ∈ {1,2,3,5} min × stop ∈ {0.375,0.5,0.75}U × target ∈ {0.75,1.0,1.5,None}U:</p>
