<h6>5.4 ★ The placebo — and a correction to how I first ran it</h6>
<p>The brief's test: shift the signal series, keep every other rule; if a fake signal books most of the money, the real one is not the edge.</p>
<p><strong>I initially ran this with shifts in both directions and I was wrong to.</strong> A <em>negative</em> shift feeds the gate the impulse that happens <strong>5 minutes in the future</strong> — that is not a placebo, it is a look-ahead oracle. Both directions are reported below, correctly labelled, because the look-ahead leg is a useful harness check (it <em>must</em> beat the real signal; if it did not, the harness would already be leaking).</p>
