<h5>7. THE L2 CHANNEL — a clean null, and one inverted surprise</h5>
<p>The book is the one channel <code>cluster()</code> genuinely cannot see (§1.5): <code>run_census.py</code> computes <code>book_depletion()</code> and prints it in the <code>book</code> column, but never passes it to <code>cluster()</code>. Per the data contract, <code>capture.db.book</code> is MNQ-only and event-driven at 41ms — correct for this section — and I read it from the lake (<code>data/tape/book/MNQ/</code>, <strong>2026-07-31 → 08-24</strong>, so 16 trading days inside the study window, not 27).</p>
<p>Aggregated to per-minute 3-deep and 10-deep bid/ask size, restricted to 13:00–15:00Z, n=22,979 5s bars:</p>
<table><tr><th>feature</th><th>what it should predict</th><th>AUC</th></tr><tr><td><code>imb3</code> = (bid₃−ask₃)/(bid₃+ask₃)</td><td>direction of the next 15 min</td><td class="num"><strong>0.508</strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>imb10</code></td><td>direction of the next 15 min</td><td class="num"><strong>0.496</strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>imb3</code></td><td>direction of the next 30 min</td><td class="num">0.509</td></tr><tr><td>`</td><td>imb3</td><td>` (magnitude of the lean)</td><td>size,</td><td>fwd15</td><td>≥ 66pt</td><td class="num">0.442</td></tr><tr><td><code>depth_z</code> (3-deep size z)</td><td>size,</td><td>fwd30</td><td>≥ 120pt</td><td class="num">0.557</td></tr><tr><td><strong><code>depth3</code> (raw 3-deep total size)</strong></td><td>size,</td><td>fwd30</td><td>≥ 120pt</td><td class="num"><strong>0.285</strong></td></tr></table>
<p><strong>Book LEAN is a coin.</strong> 0.508 and 0.496 are as close to nothing as this measurement gets, and the gate built on it (BOOKLEAN, §4.9) produced <strong>9 trades</strong> — the threshold that gives a meaningful lean almost never fires inside the US open. On non-overlapping 30-minute blocks in the book era (n=64), <code>|imb3| ≥ 0.1</code> occurs <strong>4 times</strong> and <code>≥ 0.2</code> <strong>once</strong>. There is no sample here.</p>
<p><strong>But <code>depth3</code> at AUC 0.285 is not nothing — it is inverted.</strong> Read the other way, <em>a THIN 3-deep book predicts a ≥120pt move at AUC 0.715</em>, which is better than volume-z (0.674) and better than any book <em>lean</em> measure by a mile. That is the same message as §3.2 from a third instrument: the tape tells you <strong>how big</strong>, never <strong>which way</strong>. And like <code>nt_z</code> it is a state variable — thin books cluster in time — so it inherits the same §5.4 problem and I did not build a gate on it.</p>
<p><strong>Cause of death (BOOKLEAN): n=9. Cause of death (the L2 direction channel): AUC 0.508 — no directional information at any depth or horizon.</strong></p>
<hr class="frag-sep">
<h5>8. ★ THE SIZE THRESHOLD — this is the deliverable</h5>
<p>The brief: <em>report the size-threshold at which a footprint becomes tradeable, if any — that IS the finding.</em> Here it is, three ways.</p>
<h6>8.1 The money threshold: ~120pt of follow-through</h6>
<p>MOMBRK's 52 trades, bucketed by the <strong>realised</strong> 30-minute move in the traded direction:</p>
<table><tr><th>realised follow-through</th><th>trades</th><th>% of events</th><th>net $</th><th><strong>$/trade</strong></th></tr><tr><td>≤ −60pt (went hard against)</td><td class="num">14</td><td class="num">26.9%</td><td class="num">−644.0</td><td class="num">−46.00</td></tr><tr><td>−60 … −20pt</td><td class="num">6</td><td class="num">11.5%</td><td class="num">−276.0</td><td class="num">−46.00</td></tr><tr><td>−20 … +20pt (nothing happened)</td><td class="num">9</td><td class="num">17.3%</td><td class="num">−346.0</td><td class="num">−38.44</td></tr><tr><td>+20 … +60pt</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="num">3.8%</td><td class="num">+39.5</td><td class="num">+19.75</td></tr><tr><td><strong>+60 … +120pt</strong></td><td class="num">5</td><td class="num">9.6%</td><td class="num">−20.5</td><td class="num"><strong>−4.10</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>≥ +120pt</strong></td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">30.8%</td><td class="num"><strong>+2,956.0</strong></td><td class="num"><strong>+184.75</strong></td></tr></table>
<blockquote><strong>A move of +60 to +120 points in your favour still loses money.</strong> −$4.10/trade. The 22pt stop gets tagged on the way, or the 30-minute cap arrives before the move does, or the $1.50 and the two ticks of slippage take the rest. <strong>Only follow-through beyond ~120pt pays</strong>, and when it does it pays +$184.75.</blockquote>
<p>The arithmetic that makes this a <em>rule</em> rather than an observation: with +$184.75 on a hit and −$44 on a miss, <strong>break-even hit rate = 44/(184.75+44) = 19.2%</strong>. MOMBRK's arm delivered <strong>30.8%</strong>. That 11.6-point margin is the entire edge — and §6 shows it does not survive strip-3 or OOS.</p>
<p>This lands on the same number as the desk's existing greenfield finding — <em>"the size threshold is 120pt; ≥120pt boarding pays +$69.38/tr"</em> — from a completely independent cluster and a different harness. Two independent studies converging on ~120pt on MNQ is the most durable thing on this page.</p>
<h6>8.2 The detection threshold: a footprint appears above ~120pt, sharpens above 200pt</h6>
<p>From §3.2: <code>nt_z</code> AUC runs 0.623 (55pt) → 0.638 (66) → 0.662 (80) → 0.678 (100) → <strong>0.681 (120)</strong> → 0.718 (150) → <strong>0.848 (200)</strong>. The curve is gentle to 120 and steep after 150. <strong>The escalation the brief asked for did reveal a footprint that the marginal runs wash out</strong> — and it is in the volume channel, not the price channel (<code>rng_30m</code> is flat at 0.62 across the whole range).</p>
<h6>8.3 The threshold that matters most: ~11 independent observations</h6>
<p>§3.3. On non-overlapping blocks, the ≥120pt armed sample is <strong>n=11 at 54.5% ±29.4pp</strong>. So:</p>
<blockquote><strong>The tradeable size threshold on MNQ in this window is ≈120pt of 30-minute follow-through. The footprint that predicts it is real (trade-count z, AUC 0.68 at 120pt rising to 0.85 at 200pt). The sample behind that footprint is eleven independent observations, and eleven is not enough to arm a gate on.</strong> The instrument we need is not a new measurement — it is more tape.</blockquote>
