<p>The backtest discipline forbids scoring a static config across the whole tape. Regimes are tagged <strong>causally</strong> per bar: ATR percentile-rank (trailing 2 days) × efficiency ratio over 30 minutes, in the router's own vocabulary.</p>
<blockquote><strong>A bug I fixed mid-study, reported because it would have silently deleted two regimes.</strong> My first ER summed 1-minute absolute changes at 5-second spacing — 360 <em>overlapping</em> legs — inflating the path ~12× and driving every ER to ~0.03. Under that ER, <code>clean-trend</code> and <code>building</code> <strong>did not exist anywhere in 13–15Z</strong>, and the regime table showed only the three chop buckets. Fixed to sum non-overlapping legs (median ER-30m now 0.167). Every regime number below is post-fix.</blockquote>
