<h6>12.1 What the regime table actually says</h6>
<p>The <strong>time-of-day split is far stronger than the regime split.</strong> PULSE is +$23.09/tr in 13:00–14:00Z and −$0.28/tr in 14:00–15:00Z; MOMBRK is +$51.14 and −$43.90. Within the first hour, <em>every</em> regime except trend-thin is positive; within the second, four of six are negative. Whatever this is, it is a <strong>first-hour-of-the-US-cash-session</strong> effect, not a volatility-regime effect.</p>
<p>And the regime cells that look best are the ones with no sample: normal-chop 13h is <strong>+$157/trade on 4 trades</strong>; clean-trend 13h is <strong>6 trades</strong>. Those are not home segments, they are anecdotes. The only regime cell with both a decent n and a decent number is dead-chop 13h, +$63.53 on 17 trades — and §9 has already shown that a <em>no-trigger</em> rule entering at 13:05Z makes +$47.29 on 26 trades, so even that cell is not clear of the null.</p>
<h6>12.2 ★ The router rule — stated for something that did not survive</h6>
<p>A gate that is only viable behind a router condition we cannot yet measure is a finding, not a failure. Nothing here is viable, but the honest statement of what a survivor <em>would</em> need is:</p>
<pre><code># WOULD-BE ROUTER RULE — NOT FOR DEPLOYMENT. No candidate in this section earned it.
ARM   pulse_open  WHEN  session == US_OPEN
                   AND  13:00 &lt;= utc_hour &lt; 14:00          # the SECOND hour is where it dies
                   AND  regime IN (dead-chop, normal-chop, clean-trend)   # n = 17 / 4 / 6 — NOT a sample
                   AND  nt_z(1min, 120-bucket) &gt;= 1.5      # the size footprint, AUC 0.68 at 120pt
BENCH pulse_open  WHEN  utc_hour &gt;= 14:00
                   OR   regime == trend-thin
                   OR   untradeable_meter == TRUE</code></pre>
<p>Two of those four arm conditions rest on 4 and 6 trades respectively. <strong>The router condition we cannot yet measure is not an instrument — it is sample size.</strong> We have every input this rule needs (<code>nt_z</code> is computable from <code>ticks</code> in one query, ER and ATR-rank already exist in the router's vocabulary, and the session split is free). What we do not have is 79 trading days of it.</p>
<p>If the desk wants this line of enquiry alive, the cheapest useful thing is <strong>not</strong> another gate: it is to start logging <code>nt_z</code>, <code>depth3</code> and the realised 30-min follow-through at 13:00–14:00Z every day, so that by December the ≥120pt question has n in the hundreds instead of eleven.</p>
