<h5>13. WHAT I DID NOT DO, AND WHY</h5>
<p>Stated so the absences are not read as findings.</p>
<ul><li><strong>No cross-asset (MGC) leg.</strong> MGC is $10/point and gets its own invented-fresh gates in <code>gf_MGC</code>; the contract forbids porting an MNQ gate onto gold and this section is MNQ.</li><li><strong>No V5 archive extension.</strong> <code>gaz:v5archive</code> would add MNQ history before 07-16, but the V5→V7 seam has a <strong>real tick hole 07-17 → 07-24</strong> (<code>lake.py</code> warns about it explicitly), and every candidate here needs <code>nt_z</code>/<code>vol_z</code>, which need ticks. Extending bars-only would have widened the sample for the <em>price</em> features while leaving the <em>volume</em> features — the only ones that showed a footprint — on the short sample. I judged a clean 27-day tick-complete sample better than a contaminated 40-day one. <strong>This is the single biggest thing that could change the answer</strong>, and if the seam is ever bridged, §8's eleven observations is the number to re-run first.</li><li><strong>No walk-forward re-optimisation.</strong> With 27 days and a 2-hour window there is not enough tape to split into fit/select/test three ways; the IS/OOS 2-way split in §5–6 is already thin (OOS n=10–36).</li><li><strong>No book-pressure gate beyond BOOKLEAN.</strong> The L2 direction channel measured AUC 0.508 (§7). I did not build further on a coin.</li><li><strong>The census was not re-run.</strong> <code>census_summary.json</code> and <code>census_stdout.txt</code> are read frozen, as instructed. Everything in §1–3 re-implements the census's <em>functions</em> against the lake; it does not re-cut the census's <em>run list</em>.</li></ul>
