<h5>15. VERDICT</h5>
<p><strong>NOTHING SURVIVED. Nothing ships — not to live, not to shadow.</strong></p>
<p><strong>What killed the two leaders, individually and by name:</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>MOMBRK (+$32.87/trade, n=52)</strong> — killed by <strong>strip-the-best-trades</strong> and the <strong>OOS leg</strong>. The top 3 of 52 trades are 88.5% of the net; removing them takes +$32.87 to +$4.02, and removing 5 takes it to −$11.37. Out of sample (08-17 → 08-21) it made <strong>−$16.50/trade</strong>. Seven of twenty-one days were profitable and two of them are 97% of the money. Its leave-one-day-out passed all 21 folds, which is a property of running LODO with two money days, not a clearance.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>PULSE-13h (+$23.09/trade, n=95)</strong> — killed by the <strong>placebo/shuffle test</strong>, confirmed by <strong>strip-5-best</strong> and the <strong>OOS leg</strong>. A copy of the signal delayed by 30 minutes — same window, same direction rule, same stop, same hold, just a stale trigger — books <strong>+$23.95/trade, more than the real signal's +$23.09</strong>. Stale placebos average 63% of the real signal's money. Strip 5 trades and it is −$1.89. Out of sample it made −$10.82/trade.</li></ul>
<p><strong>What killed the section:</strong> §9. A gate containing <strong>no signal at all</strong> — "enter at 13:05Z, direction = sign of the last 15 minutes, stop 0.5×U, hold 30 minutes" — books <strong>+$47.29/trade over 26 trades</strong>, double the best gate I built, and the identical rule 25 minutes later books −$13.46. Everything on this page sits inside the noise band of that control. §10 says the same thing in confidence intervals: t = 1.30 and 1.57, bootstrap 95% CIs of [−$4.14, +$26.27] and [−$2.79, +$52.71], and <strong>561 trades ≈ 79 trading days</strong> needed to resolve a $10/trade edge in this window. We have 27.</p>
<p><strong>The deliverables, which are not gates:</strong></p>
<ol><li><strong>★ The cluster label is a clock with an anti-predictive filter bolted on.</strong> The 08-15 fix correctly demoted <code>OPEN/NEWS</code> from checked-first to checked-last, taking it from 100% to <strong>58.7%</strong> of its own window. But its lift <strong>over the bare clock is 0.921×</strong> — the flow and amplitude tests remove 41% of the window and keep the <em>less</em> run-dense half. Same answer in the tick era (0.946×). Per the brief's own instruction, this finding outranks every signal on the page. <strong>Recommendation:</strong> either drop the two footprint tests from the <code>OPEN/NEWS</code> fallback and call it what it is (<code>US-OPEN-WINDOW</code>, 3.09× lift on 8.87% of tape), or route the hunt through <code>VOL-EXPANSION</code> instead — <strong>4.18× lift on 1.95% of tape</strong>, the sharpest cluster the census produces and the one it uses least.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>★ The tradeable size threshold is ≈120 points of 30-minute follow-through.</strong> Below it the gate loses even when right: +60…+120pt of follow-through still books <strong>−$4.10/trade</strong>. Above it, <strong>+$184.75/trade</strong>. Break-even hit rate is 19.2%; the best arm delivered 30.8%. This is the same ~120pt number the desk's independent greenfield work reached from a different cluster with a different harness — the most durable result on this page.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>★ Detection has a real footprint and it is VOLUME, not price; direction has none; and the footprint's honest sample is eleven.</strong> Trade-count z separates ≥200pt runs at AUC <strong>0.848</strong>, rising monotonically from 0.623 at 55pt, while 30-minute <em>range</em> is flat at 0.62 throughout — so this is not "wide days have wide runs". Direction tops out at AUC 0.55–0.65 and the crude momentum rule agrees with runs 54.2% of the time against a 53.4% base. On <strong>non-overlapping</strong> 30-minute blocks the armed sample for the ≥120pt claim is <strong>n=11 at 54.5% ±29.4pp</strong>. And the cluster's own character, in one line: <strong>PULSE and its exact mirror catch the same 6 of the 10 sat-out runs.</strong> Detection is solved. Selection is not.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>A test-design finding worth keeping.</strong> Leave-one-day-out cannot fail when k days carry the money and you only remove one. MOMBRK passed 21/21 LODO folds while two of twenty-one days held 97% of its P&amp;L. <strong>Always quote profitable-days-out-of-total next to a LODO result</strong>, and run leave-two-out when the day distribution is that skewed (MOMBRK's worst leave-two fold: +$1.19/tr).</li></ol>
