<h6>Full working, all attempts, all graves</h6>
<p><em>MNQ · tick-honest over the full Parquet lake, 2026-07-05 → 2026-08-25 (35 tape days, 45,466,604 ticks)</em> <em>Costs: MNQ $2.00/point, fee <strong>$1.50 per round trip</strong>, 1 tick (0.25pt) adverse slippage on entry and on every stop.</em></p>
<hr class="frag-sep">
<h5>0. The headline, before any signal</h5>
<p><strong>The cluster label is not a footprint. <code>FLOW-LED</code> and <code>VACUUM</code> are a coin flip, and the coin is flipped by the future.</strong></p>
<p>The census assigns <code>FLOW-LED</code> when the prior-60s net aggressor flow is unusual (|flow-z| ≥ 1.0) <strong>and its sign agrees with the FORWARD 15-minute move</strong>; <code>VACUUM</code> is the identical test with the signs disagreeing. The second half of that definition is only knowable after the run has happened. At the moment a gate would have to fire, both labels look exactly the same.</p>
<p>Measured on 43,982 minute bars of lake tape that carry a valid flow-z and a resolvable +15min close:</p>
<table><tr><th>test</th><th>result</th></tr><tr><td>base rate of the flow-event half (|fz| ≥ 1.0) on all bars</td><td><strong>20.58 %</strong></td></tr><tr><td>given a flow event, flow agrees with the next 15 min</td><td><strong>49.62 %</strong> (n = 9,022)</td></tr><tr><td>control — bars with |fz| &lt; 1.0, same question</td><td><strong>49.29 %</strong> (n = 34,786)</td></tr><tr><td>⇒ information carried by the flow event about direction</td><td><strong>0.33 percentage points</strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>FLOW-LED</code> base rate on all bars</td><td>10.21 %</td></tr><tr><td><code>VACUUM</code> base rate on all bars</td><td>10.37 %</td></tr></table>
<p>The flow event does <strong>not</strong> meet the "true on most of the tape" failure mode — 20.6 % is a real filter, and the 2026-08-01 z-score fix that replaced <code>abs(flow) &gt; 50</code> (66.5 % of bars) did its job. The label fails for a different and worse reason: <strong>the filter fires on a fifth of the tape and then splits that fifth into two almost exactly equal halves on a coin toss.</strong> <code>FLOW-LED</code> vs <code>VACUUM</code> is not two tape behaviours, it is one population cut by its own outcome.</p>
<p>Directly:</p>
<pre><code>E[fwd15 in the flow&#x27;s direction]
  |fz|&gt;=1.0   -0.299 pt   n=9,053   t = -0.61
  |fz|&gt;=1.5   +0.408 pt   n=4,594   t = +0.54
  |fz|&gt;=2.0   +0.067 pt   n=2,655   t = +0.06
  |fz|&gt;=2.5   -0.029 pt   n=1,660   t = -0.02</code></pre>
<p>Zero at every threshold, with the sign wandering. The census's own 4 <code>FLOW-LED</code> / 13 flow-event runs (30.8 % agreement) is <strong>not</strong> evidence of a contrarian tape: against the lake's 49.62 % null, P(≤4 of 13) = 0.139. Expected <code>FLOW-LED</code> among 68 census runs = 9.0, observed 4; expected <code>VACUUM</code> = 9.6, observed 9. Both inside noise. <strong>The cluster has n=4 because 68 runs is too few to populate a 10 %-base-rate label, not because the tape did something.</strong></p>
<h6>0b. Flow <em>does</em> predict magnitude — but that is a volume channel wearing a flow costume</h6>
<table><tr><th>condition</th><th>E|fwd15|</th><th>vs base</th></tr><tr><td>base (all bars)</td><td>26.70 pt</td><td class="num">1.000×</td></tr><tr><td>|fz| ≥ 1.5</td><td>33.64 pt</td><td class="num">1.260×</td></tr><tr><td>|fz| ≥ 3.0</td><td>41.73 pt</td><td class="num">1.563×</td></tr><tr><td>|volume-z| ≥ 2.0</td><td>41.75 pt</td><td class="num">1.564×</td></tr><tr><td><strong>flow unusual, volume ORDINARY</strong> (|fz|≥1.5 &amp; |volz|&lt;1.0)</td><td><strong>25.70 pt</strong></td><td class="num"><strong>0.963×</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>volume unusual, flow BALANCED</strong> (|volz|≥1.5 &amp; |fz|&lt;0.5)</td><td><strong>32.56 pt</strong></td><td class="num"><strong>1.220×</strong></td></tr></table>
<p>Strip the volume out of the flow event and the magnitude lift vanishes entirely (0.963× — below base). Strip the flow out of the volume event and the lift survives (1.220×). <strong>The census's <code>flow</code> column is a volume proxy.</strong> Net aggressor imbalance adds nothing over "a lot traded".</p>
<p>That is the strongest statement this section can make, and it outranks everything below.</p>
<hr class="frag-sep">
<h5>1. Method</h5>
<p>Everything derives from <code>ticks</code> in <code>gazbot7.lake</code> (2026-07-05 → 08-25; the documented 07-18→07-23 V5/V7 seam is absent, weekends absent — 35 tape days, 44,847 minute buckets). <code>capture.db</code> was never touched: it holds 5 trading days and would have shrunk the sample 7×.</p>
<ul><li><strong>No lookahead.</strong> A minute row at <code>ts</code> covers ticks <code>[ts, ts+60)</code>, so it is only known at <code>ts+60</code>. Every entry is stamped <code>ets = ts+60</code>. ATR is <code>.shift(1)</code>-ed off closed 5-min bars; every z-score uses <code>closed='left'</code> on a trailing 120-min window with ≥30 buckets, exactly the census recipe.</li><li><strong>Contiguity guard.</strong> <code>er30</code>/<code>brk30</code> use <code>.shift(30)</code>; across a weekend or the V5/V7 seam that silently compares two different tapes. 97.5 % of rows pass the guard; the rest are dropped, not used. (The two largest "minute moves" in the tape, 408.5pt and 295.75pt, are both 00:00:00 Monday weekend gaps — they are excluded by this guard, not traded.)</li><li><strong>Tick-honest exits.</strong> Entry at the first print ≥ <code>ets</code>, filled 1 tick adverse. Stops fill 1 tick adverse to the stop price; targets fill at the limit; the time stop fills at the print. <strong>Stop is tested before target on every print</strong> (the pessimistic ordering). One position at a time.</li><li><strong>Regimes</strong> keyed on ATR level + ER + range-break, not the clock: <code>DEAD-CHOP</code> (atr_rel&lt;0.70 &amp; er30&lt;0.30), <code>VIOLENT-WHIPSAW</code> (atr_rel≥1.6 &amp; er30&lt;0.35), <code>CLEAN-TREND</code> (er30≥0.55), <code>BUILDING</code> (0.35≤er30&lt;0.55), <code>NORMAL-CHOP</code> otherwise. Sessions ASIA / LONDON / US / LATE.</li></ul>
