<p>I am <strong>not</strong> reporting this as a survivor, for three reasons, and the operator should treat it as a lead for the structure-break phase rather than a gate:</p>
<ol><li>Its block-bootstrap 95 % CI is <strong>[−2.12, +14.36]</strong> — it straddles zero exactly as FL-4 did.</li><li>Its own IS/OOS split is +$10.38 → <strong>+$1.04</strong>/tr. Positive, but $1.04 is a third of the fee.</li><li>Its US-session leg, which is 483 of its 491 trades, goes <strong>IS +$13.64 → OOS −$2.15</strong>.</li></ol>
<p>More importantly: <strong>it is not a flow gate, and it is not this cluster.</strong> Reporting a breakout gate as the FLOW-LED cluster's finding would be the exact error the census made — attaching a flow name to something the flow had no part in.</p>
<p><strong>Router rule, if it is ever picked up by another phase</strong> (stated in live-router vocabulary so it is falsifiable): ARM when <code>atr_rel ≥ 1.4</code> (ATR-14 on 5-min bars vs its trailing 24h median) <strong>and</strong> <code>session = US</code>; BENCH otherwise; no ER condition — the ER term was measured to be worth 4 cents. Note that <code>atr_rel</code> is <strong>not currently an instrument the live router reads</strong> — the router's LAST HR ATR is a mean range, not the true-range ATR-14 this is keyed to, so arming on the router's existing number would arm on the wrong measurement. That is the instrument we would need to build first.</p>
<hr class="frag-sep">
<h5>7. What would have to be true for this cluster to be worth revisiting</h5>
<p>The FLOW-LED hypothesis is not refuted in principle — it is refuted <em>with the instrument we have</em>. The census's <code>flow</code> is a 60-second net-aggressor count from <code>ticks.aggressor</code>, and §0b shows it is a volume proxy. Three measurements would make it a fresh question rather than a repeat of this one:</p>
<ol><li><strong>Resting-liquidity flow, not print flow.</strong> <code>capture.db.book</code> is 41 ms event-driven and MNQ-only. The question worth asking is not "who crossed the spread" but "did the far side get pulled" — that is a book measurement, and it is the one the census's <code>book</code> column already gestures at.</li><li><strong>Flow at a level, not flow in a clock minute.</strong> A fixed 60-second bucket splits a single institutional order across two buckets and merges two unrelated ones. Volume-clock or order-imbalance-at-price buckets are the standard fix, and the tick data supports both.</li><li><strong>A run population large enough to populate a 10 %-base-rate label.</strong> 68 runs cannot; the lake's 5,066 bars at ≥55pt can. Any future cluster work should be labelled on the lake and only <em>illustrated</em> on the week's census.</li></ol>
