<h5>VERDICT</h5>
<p><strong>NOT SURVIVED.</strong> No FLOW-LED entry signal reached a tradeable expectancy. Nine candidates were built and all nine are dead: FL-2/3/6/7 on negative expectancy at the blanket screen, FL-1 on the <strong>OOS leg</strong>, FL-5 and FL-8 on <strong>strip-the-3-best</strong> (with FL-8 also beaten outright by its own <strong>placebo</strong>), FL-9 on the <strong>parameter sweep</strong>, and the last survivor FL-4 <code>flow_ignition</code> on the <strong>PLACEBO/SHUFFLE TEST — empirical p = 0.150, with 6 of 40 time-shifted fake flow series matching or beating it and the best fake (+$16.25/tr) beating the real signal (+$12.18/tr) outright</strong> — corroborated by a paired ablation in which the flow term's contribution inverts from +$39.43/tr in-sample to −$11.71/tr out-of-sample, and by 3/5 walk-forward folds against 5/5 for the same gate with the flow term deleted.</p>
<p><strong>There is no size threshold at which a FLOW-LED footprint becomes tradeable.</strong> On the predictor side every flow-z bar from 1.0 to 4.0 is positive in-sample and negative out-of-sample. On the outcome side, flow agreement with the run is 48.4 %–53.7 % from 55pt to 200pt and never departs from a coin flip by as much as one sigma.</p>
<p><strong>★ The finding that outranks all of the above: the cluster label itself is not a footprint.</strong> The flow-event filter fires on 20.58 % of all bars and then splits that fifth into <code>FLOW-LED</code> (10.21 % of tape) and <code>VACUUM</code> (10.37 %) on a 49.62 % coin toss — 0.33 percentage points of directional information versus the |fz|&lt;1 control. Whatever lift the flow event carries is a <strong>magnitude</strong> lift, and that lift is entirely a volume proxy: flow unusual with volume ordinary gives 0.963× base E|fwd15| (no lift at all), while volume unusual with flow balanced gives 1.220×. The census's <code>flow</code> column measures how much traded, not who was buying. <strong>Recommendation: stop splitting the run census into <code>FLOW-LED</code>/<code>VACUUM</code>.</strong> The two labels are one population cut by its own outcome, and the week's 4-vs-9 split is noise (expected 9.0 vs 9.6; P(≤4 of 13) = 0.139 against the lake null).</p>
