<h4>GREENFIELD HUNT — cluster <strong>VACUUM</strong> (census 2026-08-16 → 2026-08-21)</h4>
<p><strong>The job.</strong> Ignore every gate we own. Invent a brand-new entry signal that shows up for the runs the census filed under <strong>VACUUM</strong>, spec it mechanically, backtest it tick-honest over the <strong>full Parquet lake</strong> at the <strong>true $1.50 round-trip fee</strong>, escalate to the biggest runs if it fails, and try hard to kill it. Working below; every attempt is named, including the graves.</p>
<hr class="frag-sep">
<h5>THE THREE ANSWERS, IN ORDER OF HOW MUCH THEY MATTER</h5>
<p><strong>1. ★ The VACUUM label is not a footprint — and this week I found <em>where it comes from</em>.</strong> Last Friday's section established that the label is a coin flip. This week's larger sample (33 trading days, 43.2M ticks, 42,143 tape-minutes) confirms that and goes one step further. The flow event the label is built on fires on <strong>20.41% of every minute of tape we own</strong>. Given that event, the direction test comes up "VACUUM" <strong>49.90%</strong> of the time — against <strong>49.91%</strong> on minutes where no flow event happened at all. That is a <strong>−0.01pp</strong> difference. But the census still reports VACUUM on 15.7% of its runs, well above the 10.2% base rate, and I traced the whole of that excess to a <strong>selection artefact in <code>run_census.py</code>'s own run-picker</strong>. The picker takes every 60s-slid 15-min window over threshold and dedupes "keep-strongest", so the surviving minute is <em>by construction the local extremum of the move</em>. Rebuilding that picker on the lake: the prior-5-minute price direction agrees with the run <strong>48.66% of the time on unselected big minutes and 22.55% after the dedup — a −26.11pp shift created purely by the selection rule</strong>. The census's own 65 sat-out runs read 24.6%, matching the rebuilt picker almost exactly. Push the VACUUM condition through the same three populations and it goes <strong>10.45% → 14.01% → 21.87%</strong>. <strong>VACUUM is the name the census gives to the fact that it picked a local bottom.</strong></p>
<p><strong>2. Detection is real, it is size-graded, and it is the answer to the size-threshold question — but direction is a coin flip and I could not break it.</strong> A volume-z / ATR-expansion detector separates the biggest runs from ordinary tape at <strong>AUC 0.69 (p&lt;0.0001)</strong> on the 113 lake-wide runs of 120pt+, rising monotonically from 0.557 at 55–70pt. On the census's own top-15 the volume-z AUC is <strong>0.730, p=0.0004</strong>. Turned into a bracket gate (<strong>VAC-IGN-BRK</strong>) it catches <strong>9 of the 65 sat-out runs and 5 of the top-15 on only 48 fires in the census week — 3.6× the random-fire baseline</strong>. And it still cannot be traded, because <strong>the sign-flip control earns exactly as much as the signal</strong> (+$3.08 vs +$3.21 per trade). We can see the runs coming. We cannot tell which way they go.</p>
<p><strong>3. Last week's shadow candidate failed its forward test, and last week's one open stone is now closed.</strong> <strong>VAC-ABS</strong> reproduced to the dollar on the in-sample leg (+$24.04/tr vs the +$24.91 reported) and then lost <strong>−$529.50 over 27 trades (−$19.61/tr)</strong> on the five fresh days. Its strip-5 is <strong>−$427</strong>. It is dead, not shadowed. And the L2 far-side-depletion discriminator that last week's report nominated as "the one stone still unturned" is <strong>refuted</strong>: on 21 days and 246.9M book rows it predicts the next 15 minutes' direction at <strong>49.44% ±2.52pp</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>⚠ A method note that changed every headline in this section.</strong> My first pass let overlapping entries run concurrently. Five separate shorts booked the <em>same</em> 2026-07-31 impulse and were worth <strong>$3.9k of a $10.3k headline</strong>. A live gate takes one lot and cannot re-enter until flat. Everything below is scored <strong>one position at a time</strong>; where the unconstrained number is shown it is labelled as such and is never the verdict. Under the honest accounting VAC-IGN-BRK falls from <strong>+$10,316 / +$15.49 per trade to +$911.55 / +$3.21</strong> — <strong>91% of the apparent edge was one impulse counted five times.</strong></p>
