<h6>3.1 The three mechanical specs, for the record</h6>
<p><strong>VAC-SNAP</strong> — <em>invented here, refuted here.</em> On completed 1-min bars: <code>cumflow5</code> = Σ netflow over the last 5 bars; <code>z5</code> = its z-score against the trailing 2h of the same statistic. <strong>ARM</strong> when <code>z5 ≥ +1.5</code> (buyers) and the 5-bar price change is <code>≤ 0.35 × ATR(1m,14)</code> — heavy one-sided aggression that failed to move price. <strong>TRIGGER</strong> within 10 bars when a bar closes <strong>below the arming window's low</strong> → <strong>SHORT</strong> (mirror for sellers absorbed → LONG on a close above the window high). <strong>ENTRY</strong> first tick after that bar closes. <strong>STOP</strong> 2.0 × ATR(1m,14). <strong>EXIT</strong> stop or 30-min time-stop.</p>
<p><strong>VAC-IGN-BRK</strong> — <em>invented here, the one that detects.</em> <code>volz</code> = z-score of bar volume against the trailing 120 bars; <code>atr_ratio</code> = ATR(1m,14) averaged over 5 bars ÷ over 60 bars. <strong>ARM</strong> when <code>volz ≥ 2.0</code> <strong>and</strong> <code>atr_ratio ≥ 1.15</code>. <strong>TRIGGER</strong> within 10 bars when a bar closes outside the 5-bar range — <strong>above the high → LONG, below the low → SHORT</strong>. Non-directional by construction: the tape picks the side, the gate only picks the moment. <strong>ENTRY</strong> first tick after that bar closes. <strong>STOP</strong> 1.5 × ATR(1m,14). <strong>EXIT</strong> stop or 30-min time-stop.</p>
<p><strong>VAC-ABS</strong> — <em>last week's spec, unaltered, forward-tested.</em> <code>|z(netflow)| ≥ 3.0</code> <strong>and</strong> <code>|close − prev close| ≤ 2.75pt</code> → fade the aggressors. Stop 2.0 × ATR, 30-min time-stop.</p>
