<h5>VERDICT</h5>
<p><strong>The VACUUM cluster did NOT survive, and for the second Friday running it was killed by the LABEL itself rather than by a backtest — but this week the mechanism is identified, not just the symptom.</strong> The census's flow event fires on <strong>20.41% of every tape-minute we own</strong>, and conditional on it firing the VACUUM direction test comes up VACUUM <strong>49.90%</strong> of the time against <strong>49.91%</strong> on non-event minutes — <strong>−0.01pp</strong>, inside a ±1.1pp error bar. The apparent excess in the census (15.7% of runs vs a 10.2% base rate) is <strong>entirely a selection artefact of <code>run_census.py</code>'s keep-strongest run-picker</strong>: prior 5-min price direction agrees with the run <strong>48.66% of the time on unselected big moves and 22.55% after the dedup</strong>, and the VACUUM rate climbs <strong>10.45% → 14.01% → 21.87%</strong> across the same three populations. VACUUM is the name we give to having picked a local bottom. <strong>Traded literally (VAC-Z1) it loses −$4,150.79 over 1,768 trades serial, −$32,184 over 8,589 unconstrained.</strong></p>
<p><strong>Four candidates were invented and all four are graves, each with a named cause of death.</strong> <strong>VAC-SNAP</strong> (absorption → structural break, +$370.64 / n=410) — killed by <strong>strip-the-3-best</strong> (−$1,436) and the <strong>OOS leg</strong> (−$18.02/tr). <strong>VAC-CUMDIV</strong> — <strong>refuted outright</strong>, negative at every threshold. <strong>VAC-ABS</strong> (last week's shadow candidate, forward-tested unaltered, +$1,319.21 / n=97 / +$13.60 per trade net of $1.50 per round trip) — killed by its <strong>OUT-OF-SAMPLE LEG</strong>, −$529.50 over 27 trades on the five days it had never seen, confirmed by <strong>strip-5 = −$427</strong>; it is now <strong>RETIRED, not shadowed</strong>. <strong>VAC-IGN-BRK</strong> (the detection bracket, +$911.55 / n=284) — killed by the <strong>SIGN-FLIP CONTROL</strong>: fading the break earns <strong>+$3.08/trade against the signal's +$3.21</strong>, so both directions win and it is volatility harvesting, not edge; the parameter surface is a step rather than a plateau and 4 of 15 cells are negative.</p>
<p><strong>The size-threshold question has a real answer this week, and it is a detection threshold, not a tradeability one.</strong> Below <strong>|move| ≈ 87pt</strong> (the top-15 band) three of four detectors are indistinguishable from noise; at and above it all four go significant — volume-z <strong>AUC 0.730, p=0.0004</strong> on the census's top-15, rising lake-wide to <strong>AUC 0.867 on ATR for the 113 runs of 120pt+</strong>. <strong>VAC-IGN-BRK converts that into 9 of 65 sat-out runs and 5 of the top-15 caught on 48 fires — 3.6× the random-fire baseline, the first thing in this workstream that demonstrably shows up for the big runs.</strong> It is still not a gate, because <strong>detection without direction is a coin flip with a stop</strong>, and the sign-flip control proves it.</p>
<p><strong>Last week's one open stone is closed: the L2 far-side-depletion discriminator is REFUTED</strong> — <strong>49.44% ±2.52pp</strong> on unselected 55pt+ moves over 21 days and 246.9M book rows, <strong>49.72% ±0.67pp</strong> on all 21,249 book-minutes. Do not revive it at 30 days; the null is not n-limited.</p>
<p><strong>⚠ And one methodological finding that should outlive this section: the first pass of this backtest let overlapping entries run concurrently, and five shorts into the single 2026-07-31 impulse were worth $3.9k of a $10.3k headline. Scored one position at a time — the only way a live gate can trade — VAC-IGN-BRK falls from +$15.49 to +$3.21 per trade. 91% of the apparent edge was one impulse counted five times. Every greenfield harness on this desk should be checked for it.</strong></p>
<p><strong>Dispositions: NOTHING to LIVE. NOTHING to SHADOW. VAC-ABS retired from shadow. Two findings handed onward — (1) the census run-picker's local-extremum artefact, which invalidates every pre-run price-path statistic quoted off the run list and should be fixed or flagged in <code>run_census.py</code>; (2) the biggest runs start from CHOP (ER15 AUC 0.403), so every ER-floor arm condition the router owns is standing gates down at the moment the largest moves begin. The single cheapest next experiment is a large-lot vs small-lot aggressor split — the <code>size</code> field is already in the tick stream and no gate or census on this desk uses it.</strong></p>
