<h4>THE GOLD GATE HUNT — MGC, 2026-08-25</h4>
<p><strong>Garrath — read this paragraph and you have the week.</strong> Last Friday we shadowed a gold gate called <code>mgc_hole_break_fade</code>. It has now been running live in the shadow book since Monday, and <strong>it is losing money: −$1,196 across 80 trades in seven days, every one of its three arms red.</strong> When I replayed the same seven days in the lab it made <strong>+$512</strong>. That is not a small disagreement, and this section is mostly about running that contradiction to ground — because the answer turned out to be a single, fixable thing.</p>
<p><strong>The gate is being fed the wrong tape.</strong> The research built its one-minute bars from the <em>depth mid</em> — the midpoint of the order book, which updates every 250 milliseconds whether or not anything trades. The live service builds its bars from <em>trades</em>. Gold prints sparsely, so those are not the same series, and a sixty-minute high taken from one is not the sixty-minute high of the other. Hold absolutely everything else constant — same break rule, same book filter, same exit, same spread-honest race — and change only the input tape:</p>
<table><tr><th>the same rule, the same exit, the same race, on the six forward days both tapes cover</th><th>n</th><th>net</th><th>$/trade</th></tr><tr><td><strong>depth-mid bars</strong> (what the research measured)</td><td class="num">56</td><td class="num"><strong>+$172</strong></td><td class="num"><strong>+$3.06</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>trade bars</strong> (what the live service actually reads)</td><td class="num">53</td><td class="num"><strong>−$475</strong></td><td class="num"><strong>−$8.96</strong></td></tr></table>
<p><strong>The sign flips on the bar source alone</strong>, and the trade-bar number is the one the live shadow independently produced. So this is not a mystery any more, and it is not a research failure — it is a plumbing mismatch between the lab and production, and the fix is mechanical: the service already holds a <code>DepthFeed</code> connection to gold's order book (it needs it for the liquidity filter anyway), so it already has the bid and the ask. It just needs to build its minute bar from their midpoint instead of from trades.</p>
<p>Until that is done, <strong>I would not promote a single gold cell, and I am not proposing one.</strong> Everything below stays in shadow. But three other things came out of the week that are worth your time:</p>
