<h5>11. WHAT COULD STILL BE WRONG</h5>
<ol><li><strong>The whole reversion result may be a bar-construction artefact.</strong> §3 shows the sign flips on the input tape. My reading is that the depth mid is genuinely better information about where a level is — but the alternative reading, that the mid tape's break and the mid-derived quote race share a construction and flatter each other, is not excluded by anything I ran. <strong>A re-pointed shadow is the only clean way to settle it</strong>, which is why §3's recommendation is a build and not a claim.</li><li><strong>The forward walk leans on one day.</strong> +$341 of <code>fade_primary</code>'s +$512 is 08-25, and 08-25 is the one day with no trade-bar file to cross-check.</li><li><strong>Fourteen live trades.</strong> The two hole arms have 7 fires each. I would not conclude from that in either direction, and I have tried not to.</li><li><strong>The book is a 250ms sample, not an event stream.</strong> <code>capture.db.book</code> is 41ms and event-driven but MNQ-only. The live gate reads a slightly different book than any backtest here, in the direction of missing brief refills.</li><li><strong>The fill model assumes the touch is where the last quote said it was</strong> — in a genuine liquidity hole, which is precisely what this gate selects for, it may not be. This is why §4.3's slippage ladder matters more than any single headline, and why 3–4 ticks of headroom is the number to hold on to rather than +$11.26.</li><li><strong>The year tape has no book, and the book is where the edge is.</strong> §5 can validate the direction and nothing else. The two things I most want tested — the hole filter and the double-hole refinement — are exactly the two things 291 of those 320 days cannot speak to.</li><li><strong>The momentum cells still have no passing random-minute placebo</strong>, two weeks running, on n=63 and now n=189.</li></ol>
